9</volume><fpage>5940</fpage><lpage>5949</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16198344</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.febslet.2005.08.069</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cartwright</surname><given-names>IL</given-names></name><name><surname>Cryderman</surname><given-names>DE</given-names></name><name><surname>Gilmour</surname><given-names>DS</given-names></name><name><surname>Pile</surname><given-names>LA</given-names></name><name><surname>Wallrath</surname><given-names>LL</given-names></name><name><surname>Weber</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><name><surname>Elgin</surname><given-names>SC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Analysis of <italic>Drosophila </italic>chromatin structure <italic>in vivo</italic></article-title><source>Methods Enzymol</source><year>1999</year><volume>304</volume><fpage>462</fpage><lpage>496</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10372377</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Simon</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><name><surname>Tamkun</surname><given-names>JW</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Programming off and on states in chromatin: mechanisms of Polycomb and trithorax group complexes</article-title><source>Curr Opin Genet Dev</source><year>2002</year><volume>12</volume><fpage>210</fpage><lpage>218</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11893495</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0959-437X(02)00288-5</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Birchler</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><name><surname>Bhadra</surname><given-names>U</given-names></name><name><surname>Bhadra</surname><given-names>MP</given-names></name><name><surname>Auger</surname><given-names>DL</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Dosage-dependent gene regulation in multicellular eukaryotes: implications for dosage compensation, aneuploid syndromes, and quantitative traits</article-title><source>Dev Biol</source><year>2001</year><volume>234</volume><fpage>275</fpage><lpage>288</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11396999</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1006/dbio.2001.0262</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hilfiker</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Hilfiker-Kleiner</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Pannuti</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Lucchesi</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title><italic>Mof</italic>, a putative acetyl transferase gene related to the <italic>Tip60 </italic>and <italic>MOZ </italic>human genes and to the SAS genesof yeast, is required for dosage compensation in <italic>Drosophila</italic></article-title><source>EMBO J</source><year>1997</year><volume>16</volume><fpage>2054</fpage><lpage>2060</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9155031</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1093/emboj/16.8.2054</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Buscaino</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Kocher</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Kind</surname><given-names>JH</given-names></name><name><surname>Holz</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Taipale</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Wagner</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Wilm</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Akhtar</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>MOF-regulated acetylation of MSL-3 in the <italic>Drosophila </italic>dosag compensation complex</articl